@Xichen96 - Reviewed `1b92cc5d919bd8639873ec1d3862f61fd400fbcc`. This looks reasonable as a targeted mitigation for the observed 7215 fanout issue. The Redis setting is gated to the 7215 family, dry-run deployment remains unchanged, and failed Redis/process readiness probes are retried. No blocking code issue found.

One non-blocking follow-up: [`_fanout_cleanup_ready()`](https://github.com/sonic-net/sonic-mgmt/blob/1b92cc5d919bd8639873ec1d3862f61fd400fbcc/tests/fdb/test_fdb_churn.py#L48-L65) verifies Redis/process liveness, but does not establish that the asynchronous FDB flush has drained or that the connected uplink is operational. Please distinguish this from a complete cleanup/recovery barrier. If the gate is intended to guarantee recovery after a switching-service restart, consider adding a flush-completion check and topology-derived connected-port readiness checks, including LAG handling where applicable.

This follow-up need not block the targeted threshold mitigation and the reported exact-head validation.

